R CMD config: name the missing build tools (rzig's check mode)

src/scripts/config evaluates Makeconf through make, so without the
build tools it died with "make: not found"; pkgbuild and pak call it to
detect a compiler. First run rzig's check mode,
R_HOME/bin/toolchain/zig-cc --rzig-check=build-tools (gcc.exe on
Windows, where this script is bin/config.sh and the check also finds sh
and the binutils Makeconf.win names): it says what is missing and names
the build-tools group on stderr, and R CMD config exits with its status.
rzig ships with R on every channel (the base archive, r-zig-slim, the
r-zig wheel), so there is no other branch. feat-no-host-paths PLAN.md,
phase T; feat-standalone-toolchain PLAN.md, B26 and phase 4.

On Windows rcmdfn.c starts config.sh with `sh`, so without the build
tools cmd.exe answered "'sh' is not recognized as an internal or
external command" and R CMD config exited 1. rcmdfn.c now runs the same
check first, gcc.exe --rzig-check=build-tools with its stdout to NUL, and
returns its status (127, the build-tools group's text on stderr) when it
fails; config.sh's check then runs a second time, so the script stays one
for every OS. feat-standalone-toolchain PHASE7 open point J a.

--- a/src/scripts/config
+++ b/src/scripts/config
@@ -175,6 +175,19 @@
   R_SHARE_DIR=${R_HOME}/share
 fi
 
+## r-zig: the build tools, by rzig's check mode (feat-standalone-toolchain
+## B26): it finds make as R runs it (Windows: also sh and the binutils),
+## or names the build-tools group on stderr and exits non-zero, which ends
+## this script with its status. Its ok line goes to /dev/null: stdout is
+## the value R CMD config prints. rzig ships with R on every channel
+## (feat-standalone-toolchain phase 4). A user's hint is shown by the
+## install preflight alone (patch 0009; PHASE4 open point B b).
+if test "${R_OSTYPE}" = "windows"; then
+  rzig="${R_HOME}/bin/toolchain/gcc.exe"
+else
+  rzig="${R_HOME}/bin/toolchain/zig-cc"
+fi
+"${rzig}" --rzig-check=build-tools > /dev/null || exit
 makefiles="-f ${R_HOME}/etc${R_ARCH}/Makeconf -f ${R_SHARE_DIR}/make/config.mk"
 ## avoid passing down -jN
 MAKEFLAGS=
